<div class="scroll" style="height: 100vh; overflow-y: auto; background: var(--bg);">
  <the-marketing-nav-stub></the-marketing-nav-stub>
  <main style="max-width: 760px; margin: 0px auto; padding: 56px 40px 72px;"><span>legal</span>
    <h1 class="h1" style="margin-top: 16px;">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mono faint" style="margin-top: 10px; font-size: 12px;"> Last updated September 30, 2026</p>
    <div class="col gap-4" style="margin-top: 32px; line-height: 1.6;">
      <p class="muted"> This is a plain-language summary of what markpost collects and why. It is a draft pending owner review. </p>
      <h2 class="h2">What we store</h2>
      <ul class="col gap-2" style="padding-left: 20px;">
        <li> Your account identifier from our sign-in provider, and the Stripe customer id if you subscribe. </li>
        <li>The sources, API tokens (stored hashed), and settings you create.</li>
        <li> Everything sent to your endpoints: webhook and email payloads are converted to Markdown records and kept until you delete them or your account. </li>
        <li> An activity log of events, automatically removed after 90 days. </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="h2">Third parties</h2>
      <ul class="col gap-2" style="padding-left: 20px;">
        <li>Clerk handles sign-in and holds your email and credentials.</li>
        <li>Stripe processes payments. We never see your card details.</li>
        <li>Neon hosts the database, and Netlify hosts the app.</li>
        <li> Sentry receives error reports and performance data, which may include session replays of the app. </li>
        <li> Google Analytics (GA4) measures site usage. It loads only if you accept analytics in the consent prompt. </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="h2">Analytics choice</h2>
      <p class="muted"> Your choice is stored in this browser (local storage) and you can change it any time from the "cookie settings" link in the site footer. Declining never limits what you can do in markpost. </p>
      <h2 class="h2">Deleting your data</h2>
      <p class="muted"> Deleting your account in settings cancels billing and removes your records, sources, tokens, and settings. </p>
      <h2 class="h2">Contact</h2>
      <p class="muted"> Questions or requests: open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/neonpixels-studio/markpost"> github.com/neonpixels-studio/markpost</a>. </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <the-marketing-footer-stub></the-marketing-footer-stub>
</div>"
`;

